{"title":"Sentences to ponder","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/918837692/0/marginalrevolution~Sentences-to-ponder.html","date":1748022323000,"content":"<blockquote><p>In a landmark 2013 paper, David Autor, David Dorn and Gordon Hanson found that America lost an average of 90,000 jobs per year between 1990 and 2007 because of imports from China. But put that in perspective. <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.aei.org/op-eds/learning-the-right-lessons-from-the-china-shock/\" target=\"_blank\">According to Strain</a>, five million Americans currently separate from their employers per month. Plus, in a 2019 paper, Robert C. Feenstra, Hong Ma and Yuan Xu found that the China shock job losses were largely offset by job gains, owing to higher exports.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nytimes.com/2025/05/22/opinion/american-workers-neoliberalism-obama.html\" target=\"_blank\">more from David Brooks</a> (NYT).</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/05/sentences-to-ponder-130.html\">Sentences to ponder</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/918837692/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/918837692/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/918837692/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/918837692/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/918837